export const SEED_ORIENTATIONS: Record<string, string> = {
  "or_main": "# Operating Room (OR) — Multi-Specialty Clinical Orientation Guide\n\n## 1. Station 12 Pneumatic Tube System\nThe Main Surgical Suite uses **Station 12** for all pneumatic tube transactions.\n### CAN Be Tubed\n- Lab specimens (labeled, biohazard bag, cap secured)\n- Non-controlled medications\n- Small supply packs under 5 lbs\n\n### CANNOT Be Tubed\n- **Blood products** — Hand-carry STAT by designated runner.\n- **Controlled substances** — Dual-witness courier only.\n- **Glass containers or heavy instrument sets**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Massive Transfusion Protocol (MTP) [ROLE: RN, CRNA]\nActivation: Extension **x4-BLOOD (x4-25663)**.\nState: \"MTP activation, OR [Room], attending surgeon [Name].\"\nCooler 1 arrives in <10 min: 6 units pRBC, 4 units FFP, 1 unit Platelets (1:1:1 balanced ratio).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Malignant Hyperthermia (MH) Crisis Protocol [ROLE: RN, CRNA]\n- **MH Cart Location**: Main OR Hallway between OR 20 and OR 21 (Red labeled cart).\n- **STAT Medication**: **Ryanodex (Dantrolene)** 250mg vial reconstitutes with 5 mL sterile water.\n- **Dose**: 2.5 mg/kg IV rapid push; repeat 1 mg/kg every 5 minutes until symptoms abate.\n- **Hotline**: 1-800-644-9737 (MHAUS 24/7).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Multi-Specialty Surgical Setup & Equipment [ROLE: CIRCULATOR, SCRUB]\n- **General & Laparoscopy**: Trocars (5mm/12mm Optical), LigaSure Maryland energy sealer, Endo GIA 60mm staplers located in Cart K.\n- **Ortho & Neuro**: Stryker System 8 drill batteries in Cart L; Bone Wax and Gelfoam & Thrombin in Cart B.\n- **Cardiovascular & Vascular**: DeBakey forceps and Saphenous vein retractors (Weitlaner) in Cart J.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Nursing Documentation & Specimen Policy [ROLE: CIRCULATOR]\n- Specimen chain of custody requires dual-RN signoff before pathology runner handoff.\n- Sponge, needle, and instrument counts must be performed and documented in EHR prior to cavity closure.\n\n## Verified Peer Q&A (Crowdsourced Clinical Governance)\n- **Q: Where do we keep the backup 5-0 Prolene RB-2 sutures when Cart A Bin 3 is out during an off-shift case?**\n  - **Verified Answer**: Core Supply Cabinet D, Shelf 3, Bin B has the overflow suture box next to the vascular grafts.",
  "icu_critical_care": "# Intensive Care Unit (ICU) \u2014 Critical Care Clinical Orientation Guide\n\n## 1. Central Venous Line (CVC) & Arterial Line Standards\n- **Central Line Placement**: Full sterile drape, chlorhexidine prep 2-minute dry time, Biopatch applied blue-to-sky.\n- **Arterial Line**: Level transducer strictly to the **phlebostatic axis** (4th intercostal space, mid-axillary line). Perform fast-flush square-wave test each shift.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Continuous Renal Replacement Therapy (CRRT)\n- **Prismaflex Setup**: Prime set with 2 Liters saline. Verify replacement fluid bags and effluent scale balance.\n- **Anticoagulation**: Regional citrate anticoagulation protocol requires post-filter ionized calcium checks q2h.\n- **Fluid Warmer**: Blood warmer cuff must be positioned on the return line to prevent hypothermia.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Mechanical Ventilation & Extubation Protocols\n- **Vent Weaning SBT**: Daily Spontaneous Breathing Trial (SBT) at 0600 on PS 5 / PEEP 5 if sedation turned off.\n- **Subglottic Suctioning**: Connect ETT Hi-Lo evacuation port to continuous low wall suction (-20 to -30 mmHg).\n\n## Verified Peer Q&A (Crowdsourced Clinical Governance)\n- **Q: Where are the extra CRRT fluid warmer cuffs stored when dialysis alcove is empty?**\n  - **Verified Answer**: ICU Central Supply Room 2, Rack 4, next to the dialysis fluid totes.",
  "er_trauma": "# Emergency Department (ER) & Trauma Resuscitation Guide\n\n## 1. Trauma Activation & Code Red Resuscitation\n- **Level 1 Trauma Alert**: Page overhead and call Trauma STAT **x4-TRAUMA**.\n- **Trauma Bay Setup**: Trauma Bay 1 is reserved for unstable penetrating/blunt trauma; Bay 2 is backup/pediatric.\n- **RSI Airway Tackle Box**: Stationed at the head of bed in Bay 1 & Bay 2.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Massive Transfusion Protocol (MTP) in Emergency\n- **Rapid Cooler**: Blood bank satellite cooler staged in Alcove B. Code: **4-1-1-#**.\n- **Belmont Rapid Infuser**: Located between Trauma Bay 1 and 2. Prime with 1000mL normal saline. Target delivery up to 500 mL/min warmed to 37.5\u00b0C.\n\n---\n\n## 3. EZ-IO Intraosseous Access Protocol\n- **Anatomic Sites**: Proximal humerus (greater tubercle) or proximal tibia (2cm distal/medial to tibial tuberosity).\n- **Needle Selection**: Blue 25mm for adult tibia/humerus; Yellow 45mm for excessive tissue/adipose.\n\n## Verified Peer Q&A (Crowdsourced Clinical Governance)\n- **Q: Where is the backup EZ-IO driver when Trauma Bay 1 is missing its charger?**\n  - **Verified Answer**: Trauma Core Supply Cart T, top drawer in the yellow padded case.",
  "pacu_periop": "# PACU & Pre-Operative Care Orientation Guide\n\n## 1. Post-Anesthesia Recovery Standards & Aldrete Score\n- **Aldrete Discharge Criteria**: Minimum score of **9/10** required for Phase I discharge to floor.\n  1. **Activity**: Able to move 4 extremities spontaneously or on command (2).\n  2. **Respiration**: Able to breathe deeply and cough freely (2).\n  3. **Circulation**: BP within \u00b1 20% of pre-op level (2).\n  4. **Consciousness**: Fully awake (2).\n  5. **O2 Saturation**: SpO2 > 94% on room air (2).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Neuromuscular Reversal & Sugammadex Protocol\n- **Sugammadex (Bridion)**:\n  - Moderate block (reappearance of T2): **2 mg/kg** actual body weight.\n  - Deep block (1-2 post-tetanic counts): **4 mg/kg** actual body weight.\n  - Immediate rescue reversal after 1.2 mg/kg Rocuronium: **16 mg/kg**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Regional Anesthesia & LAST Protocol\n- **Local Anesthetic Systemic Toxicity (LAST)**:\n  - Seizure, arrhythmia, or cardiovascular collapse after nerve block.\n  - **STAT Treatment**: 20% Intralipid kit located in Pre-Op Block Alcove Pyxis. Initial bolus **1.5 mL/kg** over 1 minute.\n\n## Verified Peer Q&A (Crowdsourced Clinical Governance)\n- **Q: Where are the pediatric-size Bair Hugger gowns stored?**\n  - **Verified Answer**: PACU Supply Alcove 3, Shelf 2 in the blue labeled bin."
};

